@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Account Admin Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning account admin permissions works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | provisioning.admin                    |
	| Email Address | provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Provisioning                          |
	| Last Name     | Admin                                 |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Admin"
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Rchild - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Perpro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Misper - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the fourth default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Permission Partner |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| RCHILDRCHILD |
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| PERPROPERPRO |
	| MISPER       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Rchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Perpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| RCHILDRCHILD |
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| PERPROPERPRO |
	| MISPER       |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Rchild - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Perpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId4}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: Add address
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and adding an additional address in the provisioning page account details

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I create a team with the name "Permission Partner" for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "Permission Partner" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	When I click on the "Details" tab
	And I click the add account address button in position "1"
	And I edit the following account address fields and types in position "2" to the following values under the account details tab
	| Street 1       | Input         | 456 Main Street  |
	| Country        | Select        | Canada        	|
	| City           | Input         | Vancouver        |
	| State/Province | Select        | British Columbia |
	| Postal Code    | Input         | V5Y 0C9          |
	| Primary        | Toggle Switch | false            |
	Then I should be able to view the following account values under the account details tab
	| Account Name        | Permis - ${staticProjectName} |   |
	| State               | ACTIVE                        |   |
	| Code                | MISPERPERMIS                  |   |
	| Tier                | T4                            |   |
	| Parent              | Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |	  |
	| Data Region         | United States                 |   |
	| First Line Support  | Permission Partner            |	  |
	| Street 1            | 456 Fake Street               | 1 |
	| Country             | United States                 | 1 |
	| City                | Diamond Bar                   | 1 |
	| State/Province      | California                    | 1 |
	| Postal Code         | 91765                         | 1 |
	| Primary             | true                          | 1 |
	| Street 1            | 456 Main Street               | 2 |
	| Country             | Canada                        | 2 |
	| City                | Vancouver                     | 2 |
	| State/Province      | British Columbia              | 2 |
	| Postal Code         | V5Y 0C9                       | 2 |
	| Primary             | false                         | 2 |
	| Dossiera Project    | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}   |   |
	| Salesforce Project  | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |   |
	And I should be able to view a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the street address "456 Main Street" with the following values
	| Country               | Canada           |
	| Locality              | Vancouver        |
	| Region                | British Columbia |
	| Mailing               | false            |
	| Postal Code           | V5Y 0C9          |
	| Primary               | false            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 456 Main Street  |
	And I should be able to view a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the street address "456 Fake Street" with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Mailing               | false           |
	| Postal Code           | 91765           |
	| Primary               | true            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 456 Fake Street |
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Address" with the field value "Address" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Address |
	| Update Field Name           | Address              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | 456 Fake Street      |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Address" with the field value "Address" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Address          |
	| Update Field Name           | Address                       |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | Diamond Bar, California 91765 |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Auto > Added Address" with the field value "Address" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added Address |
	| Update Field Name           | Address              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                  |
	| Update Field New Value      | United States        |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Address" with the field value "Address" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Address |
	| Update Field Name           | Address                            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                |
	| Update Field New Value      | 456 Main Street                    |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Address" with the field value "Address" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Address  |
	| Update Field Name           | Address                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | Vancouver, British Columbia V5Y 0C9 |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Added Address" with the field value "Address" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Added Address |
	| Update Field Name           | Address                            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                |
	| Update Field New Value      | Canada                             |

Scenario: Delete address
	Testing the ability to create a T4 project in Dossiera and deleting the project address in the provisioning page account details

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	And I create a team with the name "Permission Partner" for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "Permission Partner" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	When I click on the "Details" tab
	And I delete the account address in position "1"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Details" tab
	Then I should be able to view the following account values under the account details tab
	| Street 1            | -     | 1 |
	| Country             | -     | 1 |
	| City                | -     | 1 |
	| State/Province      | -     | 1 |
	| Postal Code         | -     | 1 |
	| Primary             | false | 1 |
	And I should not be able to view a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the street address "456 Fake Street"
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Deleted Address" with the field value "Address" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Deleted Address |
	| Update Field Name           | Address                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | 456 Fake Street                      |
	| Update Field New Value      | N/A                                  |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Deleted Address" with the field value "Address" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Deleted Address |
	| Update Field Name           | Address                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | Diamond Bar, California 91765        |
	| Update Field New Value      | N/A                                  |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Deleted Address" with the field value "Address" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Deleted Address |
	| Update Field Name           | Address                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | United States                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | N/A                                  |

Scenario: Update account
	Testing the ability to update a T4 account in Provisioning and viewing the project in the provisioning page account details 

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	Then the support organization with the code "MISPERPERMIS" should be part of the support site
	And I create an external link for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | analytics-cloud |
	| Entity Id   | 67890           |
	| Entity Name | group           |
	And I create an external link for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
